	"Name": "Witchy Alternative Tools",
	"Author": "demobatty",
	"Description": "[font=Courier New][size=5]Hihi!\u00A0[/size]\n<br />\n<br />   [size=4]\uFEFFThis is a retexture for the tools in Alternative Textures to make them a little more fantasy than modern! I got permission from PeacefulEnd to retexture them and I'm so proud of my silly little mod! I initially made one color but then chose to make a few colorways!(the blue one specifically was made with my friend's Joja Route in mind lol)[/size]\n<br />\n<br />   \uFEFFThat in mind, please choose [i]ONE[/i]\u00A0color! You can mix and match if you want to pick through the PNGs as you please, but you cannot use all the textures at once :]\n<br />\n<br />   [size=4]\uFEFFWith these, your paint bucket will become a cauldron, the paint brush to a crystal wand, the catalogue to a grimoire, scissors to a potion and finally the spray can into a crystal ball! The Spray Can does also have a \"Rare\" variant included and the paint brush does have an empty/filled sprite, though the one pictured is when it is \"Filled\" &lt;3[/size]\n<br />\n<br />   \uFEFF   [size=2]ps. If I manage to figure out how Content Patcher for non-vanilla textures works, there will be a CP version with (hopefully) GMCM compatibility, but that's for future me to worry about[/size]\n<br />[/font]\n<br />\n<br />[font=Courier New][size=5]Instructions:[/size]\n<br />   [size=4]1. Download your chosen colorway and Unzip the folder\n<br />   \uFEFF2. Open the Alternative Textures mod and navigate to the Assets folder [AlternativeTextures&gt;Framework&gt;Assets]\n<br />   \uFEFF3. Copy all the witchy textures into the Assets folder and [i][b]REPLACE[/b][/i] all 7\u00A0\n<br />   \uFEFF4. Done!![/size][/font]",
